# cargo-fuzz build output and machine-discovered data (working corpora, crash artifacts,
# coverage). These are VOLATILE: cargo-fuzz rewrites the working `corpus/<target>/` on every
# run, so they are never committed. Cargo.lock IS committed for reproducible nightly soaks,
# matching this repo's supply-chain rigor.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/

# ...but the committed, content-addressed REGRESSION corpus (#385) IS tracked: it is the
# permanent seed set (the frozen #45 conformance vectors + crafted hostile inputs, plus any
# promoted minimized crasher) that the per-PR smoke and the nightly soak replay. The `corpus/`
# rule above matches only a path component named exactly `corpus`, so `corpus-regression/` is
# already tracked; this negation is belt-and-suspenders and documents the intent. Re-seed with
# `sh fuzz/seed-regression-corpus.sh`.
!corpus-regression/
!corpus-regression/**
